<title>USA: Westmoreland says mulling bankruptcy.</title>
<headline>Westmoreland says mulling bankruptcy.</headline>
<dateline>COLORADO SPRINGS, Colo. 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westmoreland Coal Co said on Thursday that it is examining alternatives, including court protection under Chapter 11 of the U.S. Bankruptcy Code.</p>
<p>Westmoreland said that company-initiated discussions with United Mine Workers of America Pension and Benefit Funds aimed at a settlement of over $160 million in retiree benefit obligations remained unsuccessful.</p>
<p>The company said that in light of continuing demands and litigation by the Funds to force Westmoreland to make payments beyond its financial capacity, it was examining alternatives.</p>
</text>
